Now, `put` in full:

```rust
pub fn put(&mut self, key: K, value: V) -> Option<V> {
    if let Some(&i) = self.map.get(&key) {
        self.unlink(i);
        let old = std::mem::replace(&mut self.nodes[i].value, value);
        self.attach_head(i);
        return Some(old);
    }
    if self.nodes.len() == self.capacity {
        debug_assert!(self.tail.is_some(), "capacity is at least 1 and cache is full");
        let t = self.tail.unwrap();
        let _ = self.remove_node(t);
    }
    self.insert_head(key, value);
    None
}
```

`unlink` and `attach_head` are as above. Note: in the existing-key case, `unlink(i)` when i is the only node: head=None, tail=None; attach_head: old_head None, head=Some(i), tail None→Some(i). Good.

