5 failures, all index-out-of-range or ordering issues. Let me trace the bug.

Failure: `pop_lru` test — panic "len is 1 but the index is 1" at line 143. Line 143 is inside the fixup of `remove_node`… let me look at the current file's lines to confirm.

Let me trace `remove_node` very carefully.

```rust
fn remove_node(&mut self, i: usize) -> (K, V) {
    self.unlink(i);

    let removed = self.nodes.swap_remove(i);
    let last = self.nodes.len();
    if last != i {
        let prev = self.nodes[i].prev;
        let next = self.nodes[i].next;
        if let Some(p) = prev {
            self.nodes[p].next = Some(i);
        } else {
            self.head = Some(i);
        }
        if let Some(n) = next {
            self.nodes[n].prev = Some(i);
        } else {
            self.tail = Some(i);
        }
        self.map.insert(self.nodes[i].key.clone(), i);
    }
    self.map.remove(&removed.key);
    (removed.key, removed.value)
}
```

